{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-full-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:06:55.290Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d18c62d5310f850b9d7cb1ceb05cfc109aa5c51733eb9bea445f0871d8a94e08","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three tickets. None of them sits next to the name \"Marrow Fieldworks\" in so many words, so I've noted how I tied each one to the account.\n\n1. **#4409**, from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (2 Jan 2026, team-central digests). The Gatehouse Check-In report keeps timing out at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n2. **#4412**, from the same digest. A minor glitch in the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n   - Why I linked 4409 and 4412: the digest lists them as Hollis's open tickets \"on Pree's dealer account\", right under the line saying Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan.\n3. **#8841**, from #central-random (13 Oct, your own message). West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk.\n   - Why I linked it: Hollis asked about \"Tobias's dealer account\", and you answered about the Plains depots. I'm assuming that's the same dealer account after the January handoff, but nothing I can see says so outright.\n\n**Left out on purpose:**\n- **FR-882** (same digest) is a feature request from **Marrow Agrisupply**, which is a separate account.\n- Pree's IT lockout ticket and the Quarrendon tickets (#4419, #PD-4492) have nothing to do with Marrow.\n\n**Couldn't find:** there's no Marrow Fieldworks account folder that you can access, and Moss's other notes don't mention it. If the CRM has more tickets, they're not anywhere you or I can see."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
